-- The primitive solutions of d⁴ = a⁴ + b⁴ + c⁴ with d < 10^30 that were not
-- yet on the site: 152 of the 179 in Matej Veselovac's credited list, sent by
-- email on 2026-10-05 (it extends his table at math.stackexchange.com/a/5150609).
-- Each identity was verified with exact BigInt arithmetic and is primitive.
-- Purely additive: a row is skipped if its identity is already present.
--
-- Credit follows the list, which credits the oldest source of each solution;
-- a "pair" there is the partner solution on the same elliptic curves
-- (math.stackexchange.com/q/4857229). Dates are the earliest dated
-- appearance found, read 2026-10-07: the revision history of the MSE posts
-- the list cites, Tomita's dated table (dioph225e), the commit history of
-- Roger Frye's repository and Hisayasu Nakao's page (stamped 2024-11-20).
-- Each row links that earliest source. When the list's year is earlier than
-- every dated source (Bremner 2013, Berg 2025), the date is 1 January of
-- that year. Four of Veselovac's solutions were unpublished and take the
-- date of the email. Five rows credited only as "pair of X" take X and the
-- date of the partner solution.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO contributors (name) VALUES
  ('Seiji Tomita'),
  ('Matej Veselovac'),
  ('Roger Frye'),
  ('Tito Piezas III'),
  ('Andrew Bremner'),
  ('Hisayasu Nakao'),
  ('Dan Fulea'),
  ('Anders Berg');

